        "learnerExperience": "In groups of four, learners conduct a concentric circular cut-out investigation (about 12 minutes). Each group receives two pre-drawn concentric circles on card (outer radius R = 12 cm, inner radius r = 8 cm), scissors, a ruler and a calculator. Step 1, Measure: learners measure and record R and r. Step 2, Cut: they cut out the full outer circle, then the inner circle, giving a ring-shaped piece (the annulus) and a small disc. Step 3, Record in a table: (a) area of the full outer circle πR², (b) area of the inner disc πr², and (c) area of the ring written as Area_ring = Area_outer − Area_inner. Step 4, Generalise: each group writes one sentence describing the pattern and labels on the Laikipia photograph which part of the irrigation system is R and which is r.",
