        "teacherMoves": "Begin by asking: 'Who can give me one sentence that captures what we found?' (WAIT TIME 12 seconds) Cold-call the group whose sentence was scribed. Write on the board: 'Area of annulus = Area of outer circle − Area of inner circle = πR² − πr² = π(R² − r²).' Say: 'We can also factorise: π(R − r)(R + r). It makes mental arithmetic easier: 120² − 80² = 40 × 200 = 8000.' Do NOT spend more than 1 minute on the factorisation. Display Problem 1 and say: 'Work this out individually. You have 4 minutes. Show every substitution step.' After 4 minutes: 'Compare with your partner. If you disagree, find where the difference began.' Cold-call 2 pairs to present and invite the class to agree or challenge. Ask: 'How many hectares of maize can the farmer water with just the ring? How does this help with planning seed or fertiliser?' Take 2 responses. Say: 'Next lesson we look at the wedge the pivot sweeps, which needs a different approach.' Offer Problem 2 to early finishers; set it as homework for the rest. Accommodations: learners may show their working orally, as a labelled sketch, or in writing; give large-print diagrams to learners with low vision and pre-cut inner circles to learners with fine-motor difficulty.",
