        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Take out your circle model. Add the hatch and the major segment, in a different colour so that the growth of your model is visible.' Give 4 minutes and circulate; look for the shaded minor segment, the major-segment annotation, and the correct use of cm². Ask a learner who only writes the formula: 'Which region does your arrow point to, the small piece or the big piece?' In the last minute cold-call 2 learners to read their 'before/after' note. Hand-off: 'Bring the Lesson 7 stencils: two circles will overlap and we will find out what the shared region is made of.'",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative annotated model revision (NGSS SEP 2: Developing and Using Models). The running diagram functions as a personal knowledge-building artefact — each lesson's addition is visually connected to previous sub-regions, reinforcing that sectors, annuli, annular sectors, and segments are all decompositions of the same circle. Anchoring the minor and major segments to a thumbnail of the Turkana hatch makes the abstraction concrete and memorable.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Check each model for: (a) the hatch segment correctly shaded (not the whole sector); (b) the 'Major segment = πr² − minor segment' annotation; (c) the before/after note. Learners who shade the same region for minor and major segments need a quick re-teach at the start of Lesson 7."
