    "overview": "Learners recall the Lesson 7 results (AM = 30 m, MB = 19 m, angles 88.83° and 114.24°) and revisit the Prediction Bank. They check the calculated angles against their own A3 traces with a protractor. In the Explain phase the teacher completes the derivation (the two segment areas and their sum), and pairs practise the six steps on the Kericho tea-estate plots. The DQB is updated to flag that all major sub-regions of a circle have now been covered. Learners close by completing their cumulative model with the lens formula and a Model Upgrade Note. Pacing for a 40-minute period: Predict 4, Observe 7, Explain 19, Driving Question Board 3, Model Building 7.",
