    "teacherReflection": "After the lesson, reflect on the following questions: (1) Prediction Bank: how close were the predictions to 1 148 m²? Which strategy (subtract full circles, rectangle approximation, two segments) did the closest learners use? (2) Common errors: did learners confuse the half-angle (α) with the full central angle (2α) when substituting into the segment formula? Document how many pairs made this error during Part B and whether the in-flight prompt ('Which angle is at the centre of the sector?') was sufficient. (3) Time: did 13 minutes suffice for the Kericho problem? If not, use it as homework and take the answers at the start of Lesson 9. (4) Did the protractor check in the Observe phase help, or were the traces too inaccurate? (5) DQB quality: were CLAIM notes specific enough to reference the lens formula by name? If not, add the sentence stem 'I can now calculate ___ using the formula ___.' (6) Phenomenon connection: did learners connect the 1 148 m² answer to the Laikipia farmers' shared water bill?",
