      "purposeInStoryline": "In Lessons 1–8 the farmer's field was decomposed into annuli, sectors, annular sectors, segments and the lens between two plots. In Lessons 9 and 10 the farmer must make integrated plans that combine two or more of these. Lesson 9 takes the first two problems: a Nakuru maize plot (annular sector minus a segment) and a Nairobi urban farm (circle minus a segment). Lesson 10 takes a Mombasa fish-pond problem and a Laikipia fencing plan, and holds the peer-assessment gallery for all four.",
