    "teacherReflection": "After the lesson, reflect on the following questions: (1) Did groups find that the inward sector in Problem 4 completes the circle (so the answer is a quarter of the R = 42 m circle, 1 386 m²), or did they compute the two parts separately? Both are correct. (2) Peer assessment quality: were the Peer Assessment Cards specific, or vague? If vague, give the sentence-stem card 'The formula used was ___, but it should have been ___, because ___.' in Lesson 11. (3) FORMULA COMBINATION ERRORS: what was the single most common multi-step error across Lessons 9 and 10? Prepare one warm-up question for Lesson 11. (4) Did 4 minutes for the composite figure suffice? Learners may complete it at home. (5) MODEL COMPLETENESS: how many learners' models contain entries for all ten lessons? Plan a 5-minute peer model review at the start of Lesson 12 for those with gaps.",
