        "learnerExperience": "Self-marking and error tally (about 6 minutes). The teacher reads the model answers aloud (or shows them on the board): Q1: π(45²−30²) = π(2025−900) = 1125π ≈ 3534.29 m²; Q2: (135/360)×π×45² = (3/8)×2025π = 759.375π ≈ 2385.65 m²; Q3: (135/360)×π×(45²−30²) = (3/8)×1125π ≈ 1325.36 m²; Q4: (80/360)×π×20² − ½×20²×sin80° = (2/9)×400π − 200×0.9848 ≈ 279.25 − 196.96 ≈ 82.29 m²; Q5: the common chord meets the line of centres at its midpoint M (equal radii), so AM = 15 m and PM = √(25² − 15²) = 20 m; cosα = 15/25 = 0.6, α = 53.13°, 2α = 106.26°; each segment = (106.26/360)×π×25² − PM × AM = 579.56 − 20 × 15 = 579.56 − 300 ≈ 279.56 m²; total ≈ 559.12 m². Learners self-mark against the model answers, tick or cross each question, and write beneath the test the question numbers they got wrong and the likely reason (wrong formula, substitution error, arithmetic error, or missing step).",
